#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:152
msgid "TalentTrack — demo data template"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:154
msgid "How to fill this workbook"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:155
msgid "Each green tab is a master entity (Teams, People, Players, Trial cases). Each blue tab is a transactional record (Activities, Attendance, Evaluations, Goals, Player journey). Purple = settings, grey = reference."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:157
msgid "auto_key (the first column on every entity tab)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:158
msgid "Type a short, unique label (e.g. \"ABC\", \"U12_RED\", \"MARTIN\") in the auto_key cell. Other tabs reference back to it via team_key / player_key / session_key fields. The importer maps your auto_key to the inserted row id, so cross-sheet links resolve at import time without you needing the database id."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:159
msgid "Leave auto_key blank if you do not need to reference the row from another sheet — but most rows are referenced somewhere, so filling it in is the safe default."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:161
msgid "Foreign-key columns (e.g. team_key, player_key)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:162
msgid "Type the auto_key value of the row you want to link to. Example: a Players row with team_key=\"ABC\" links to the Teams row whose auto_key is \"ABC\". The importer rejects the workbook if a foreign-key value points to a row that does not exist."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:164
msgid "Importable vs. documentation-only sheets"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:165
msgid "The importer (v1.5) consumes: Teams, People, Players, Trial_Cases, Activities, Session_Attendance, Evaluations, Evaluation_Ratings, Goals, Player_Journey, Generation_Settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:166
msgid "Reference tabs (Eval_Categories, Category_Weights, _Lookups) are documentation-only. Configure those via the wp-admin Configuration screens. They are included here so you can see what categories / weights / lookups your imported data will key into."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:168
msgid "Required vs. optional columns"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:169
msgid "Every column header carries a label. Required columns are typically the human-name fields (first_name / last_name / title) plus the foreign keys that establish relationships. The importer will tell you which row + column failed validation when you upload."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:171
#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:254
#: src/Modules/Trials/Wizards/TrialStaffStep.php:114
#: src/Shared/Frontend/FrontendTournamentsManageView.php:344
msgid "Dates"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:172
msgid "YYYY-MM-DD only. Excel sometimes auto-formats dates to your local format on cell entry — set the column format to \"Text\" first if you see weird date values after upload."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:174
msgid "Recommended workflow"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:175
msgid "1. Fill Teams first. Pick auto_key labels that mean something to you (\"U12_RED\", \"U14_GREEN\")."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:176
msgid "2. Fill People next, referencing Teams via team_key on staff rows."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:177
msgid "3. Fill Players, referencing Teams via team_key."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:178
msgid "4. Add Activities for each team (they reference Teams via team_key)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:179
msgid "5. Add Session_Attendance rows for who showed up at each activity."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:180
msgid "6. Add Evaluations + Evaluation_Ratings, referencing Players + Activities."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:181
msgid "7. Add Goals + Player_Journey events as needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:183
msgid "Save as .xlsx and upload via TalentTrack → Configuration → Demo data → Step 0 — Source → Excel upload."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:242
msgid "TalentTrack — squad template"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:244
msgid "What to fill in"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:245
msgid "Three tabs: Teams, Players and People. Fill Teams first, then Players, then People — the later tabs point back at the teams you named."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:247
msgid "auto_key (the first column on every tab)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:248
msgid "Type a short, unique label (e.g. \"U12_RED\", \"U14_GREEN\") in the auto_key cell on the Teams tab. Players and People then reference that label in their team_key column, which is how each person ends up in the right team."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:249
msgid "Leave auto_key blank on a row nothing else needs to point at."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:251
msgid "Staff go on the People tab"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:252
msgid "Coaches, assistants and other staff are People rows. Give each one a role and a team_key so they arrive attached to the team they work with."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:255
msgid "YYYY-MM-DD only. Excel sometimes reformats dates as you type them — set the column format to \"Text\" first if dates look wrong after upload."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:257
msgid "Before anything is saved"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Import/Excel/TemplateBuilder.php:258
